{"answer": "The SRPN field defines the **Service Request Priority Number**, i.e. the priority of a service request relative to other service requests with the same service provider (same SRC.TOS configuration). `00H` is the lowest priority and `FFH` is the highest priority. [S2]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-mini", "question": "What does the SRPN field define in the SRC register?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 6, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1370, "page_start": 1370, "score": -0.031099324975891997, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 8}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 3, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1367, "page_start": 1367, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 8, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1371, "page_start": 1371, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}], "timestamp": "2026-05-25T17:42:04.279864+00:00", "top_k": 3}
{"answer": "To change `SRC.TOS` or `SRC.SRPN` for an enabled SRN, use this sequence: disable the SRN (`SRC.SRE=0`), verify it is disabled, poll `LWSRx` until the pending request is no longer present per the documented condition, then modify `SRC.TOS` and/or `SRC.SRPN`, and finally re-enable the SRN (`SRC.SRE=1`) [S1].", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-mini", "question": "What sequence is required to change SRC TOS or SRPN for an enabled Service Request Node?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 6, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1370, "page_start": 1370, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 10, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1373, "page_start": 1373, "score": -0.03225806451612903, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 8, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1371, "page_start": 1371, "score": -0.03125, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}], "timestamp": "2026-05-25T17:43:42.595727+00:00", "top_k": 3}
{"answer": "SETR and CLRR are software control bits used to set or clear the Service Request Flag SRR in the Service Request Control Register. Writing `1` to SETR sets SRR to `1`, and writing `1` to CLRR clears SRR to `0`. If both are written as `1` at the same time, SRR is not changed. [S1][S2]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-mini", "question": "What is the purpose of SETR and CLRR in the Service Request Control Register?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 9, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1372, "page_start": 1372, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 4, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1368, "page_start": 1368, "score": -0.03225806451612903, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": null, "chunk_index": 3, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1367, "page_start": 1367, "score": -0.03149801587301587, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}], "timestamp": "2026-05-25T17:44:54.410492+00:00", "top_k": 3}
